Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::a_lockup_bit_is_never_overridden`.

The defect: `generation_outcome` lets `RAND_RDY` outrank `LFSR_LOCKUP`, by taking the lockup arm only when
`RAND_RDY` is clear. The lockup latch is then ignored whenever a result is also standing, so bytes
from a core that reported a single-event upset are served as clean.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(generation_outcome(status, interrupt_status, random_numbers), GenerationOutcome::Lockup)`: with both bits set (and
the core seeded) `generation_outcome` returns `Ready`.

